{"nodes": [{"id": "public_apple_touch_icon", "label": "apple-touch-icon.png", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "public/apple-touch-icon.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "public_apple_touch_icon_dumbbell_glyph", "label": "Orange dumbbell (barbell) glyph", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "public/apple-touch-icon.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "public_apple_touch_icon_ios_home_screen_icon", "label": "iOS Home Screen icon (apple-touch-icon)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "public/apple-touch-icon.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Facts: README's iPhone install flow is Safari > Share > Add to Home Screen > 'Launch from the icon'; index.html L11 has <link rel='apple-touch-icon' href='./apple-touch-icon.png'>; vite.config.ts L34 lists it in vite-plugin-pwa includeAssets; it is NOT in the manifest icons (those are icons/icon-192, icon-512 and maskable-512, for Android/Chromium installs). Inferred rationale: iOS Safari takes the Home Screen tile from the apple-touch-icon link, so a dedicated 180x180 opaque full-bleed PNG is shipped (iOS applies its own rounded-corner mask, hence no baked-in corners and no alpha channel)."}, {"id": "public_apple_touch_icon_brand_palette", "label": "Icon palette (#0B0F14 dark + #F97316 orange)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "public/apple-touch-icon.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Measured from pixels: about 80% of the canvas is #0B0F14 and the glyph is #F97316. #0B0F14 equals Tailwind 'bg' (tailwind.config.js L7), the PWA manifest theme_color/background_color (vite.config.ts L46-47) and <meta name='theme-color'> (index.html L10); #F97316 equals Tailwind 'primary' (orange-500, tailwind.config.js L14). Inferred rationale: the Home Screen tile matches the in-app dark theme and brand accent. The colours are baked into the PNG pixels of all four icon files, so changing those tokens means regenerating the icons by hand."}], "edges": [{"source": "public_apple_touch_icon", "target": "public_apple_touch_icon_dumbbell_glyph", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "public/apple-touch-icon.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "public_apple_touch_icon", "target": "public_apple_touch_icon_brand_palette", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "public/apple-touch-icon.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "public_apple_touch_icon_ios_home_screen_icon", "target": "public_apple_touch_icon", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "public/apple-touch-icon.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "index", "target": "public_apple_touch_icon", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "public/apple-touch-icon.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vite_config", "target": "public_apple_touch_icon", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "public/apple-touch-icon.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "public_apple_touch_icon_brand_palette", "target": "tailwind_config", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "public/apple-touch-icon.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "public_apple_touch_icon_brand_palette", "target": "vite_config", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "public/apple-touch-icon.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "